Applies the PR #417 review findings:

- BLOCKER: loadSkillCatalog/loadDispatchText read from the Forge PACKAGE root
  (getPackageRoot: npm dir or compiled-binary embedded assets), NOT projectRoot.
  A set-up consumer project has no root skills/ (only mirrors), so the feature was
  a no-op outside the source checkout. Callers (hooks session-start, skill router)
  now resolve the package assets; an explicit override stays for tests.
- MAJOR: collectPrimeLiveState is now strictly read-only — gated on an ALREADY-
  EXISTING Kernel DB (resolveKernelDatabasePath only computes a path), so `forge
  prime` in a fresh repo never lazily creates/migrates the DB.
- MAJOR: prime now LEADS with live state — prepended to the COMPLETE orientation and
  prioritized to sort first (sections[0].id == live_state).
- MAJOR: routeSkill only scores skills present in the catalog; an empty/unavailable
  catalog returns no matches (unknown:true) instead of fabricating skill names.
- MAJOR: refactored using-forge (frontmatter/catalog/router) into small helpers for
  the cognitive-complexity gate; behavior identical.
- MINOR: injectable snapshot seam (_readSnapshot/_workflowState) + tests for the
  activeAssigned->claimed{id,title} / ready->readyCount mapping and no-DB-creation.

Tests paired to convention: using-forge-router.test.js -> using-forge.test.js (pairs
lib/using-forge.js); new test/commands/skill.test.js pairs lib/commands/skill.js.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
